Z||000000||olliver||10-17-2001||02:55 PM||||Talk about a bad case of the gremlins.  First of all lets start off with the basics.  I just had my 2.8L rebuilt by my cousin's race shop and now i've just had one problem after another.  <P>1.  Had EXCESSIVE fuel consumption.  So i shipped my injectors off to a company in edmonton to get them rebuilt.  There were 2 injectors that were completely different.  They didn't have the nice black cap on the end they looked like hollow tube and had 6 pin holes inside.  The guy said when he hooked them up (those 2) they shot out like a garden hose.  Purchased 2 rebuilt injectors and installed them.<P>2.  I need to know the rev's at various speeds.  My car has the 3 speed auto and i think it's revving quite high something like 3000 rpm @ 100km/h.  Can anyone tell me what rpm the engine should be running at different speeds. (100 - 200 km/h)<P>3. I've removed the factory air box and installed a 3" bent tube to the side scoop.  Now just thinking about this, will that not drop vacuum pressure inside the intake plenum giving false readings to the ecm?  And exactly how much vacuum should there be @ idle?<P>4.  What is the number one cause of the tcc not engaging?  I know for a fact that mine does not engage.<P>Please all my fiero luvin' brothers and sisters i'm in desperate need of your help!<P>Thank you,<BR>olliver<BR>P.S. elvis has now left the building<P>||||reg||4
Z||000001||Joe Torma||10-17-2001||03:15 PM||||I guess I know about a couple of your problems...<P>1.  Had EXCESSIVE fuel consumption.  <P>Seems like someone decided to swap out your original pintle injectors for the later model disc(that probably were bad).  <P>3. I've removed the factory air box and installed a 3" bent tube to the side scoop<P>I've done the same thing...so have many fiero people...and every ricer has one.  Adds like 50 hp you know.<P>My 3400 pulls 11"Hg at idle...but I'm sure this differs with timing and a half dozen variables.<BR> <P>4.  What is the number one cause of the tcc not engaging?  I know for a fact that mine does not engage.<P>Dunno...solinoid busted?  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Seanh||10-17-2001||04:01 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by olliver:<BR><B>Talk about a bad case of the gremlins.  First of all lets start off with the basics.  I just had my 2.8L rebuilt by my cousin's race shop and now i've just had one problem after another.  <P>1.  Had EXCESSIVE fuel consumption.  So i shipped my injectors off to a company in edmonton to get them rebuilt.  There were 2 injectors that were completely different.  They didn't have the nice black cap on the end they looked like hollow tube and had 6 pin holes inside.  The guy said when he hooked them up (those 2) they shot out like a garden hose.  Purchased 2 rebuilt injectors and installed them.<P>2.  I need to know the rev's at various speeds.  My car has the 3 speed auto and i think it's revving quite high something like 3000 rpm @ 100km/h.  Can anyone tell me what rpm the engine should be running at different speeds. (100 - 200 km/h)<P>3. I've removed the factory air box and installed a 3" bent tube to the side scoop.  Now just thinking about this, will that not drop vacuum pressure inside the intake plenum giving false readings to the ecm?  And exactly how much vacuum should there be @ idle?<P>4.  What is the number one cause of the tcc not engaging?  I know for a fact that mine does not engage.<P>Please all my fiero luvin' brothers and sisters i'm in desperate need of your help!<P>Thank you,<BR>olliver<BR>P.S. elvis has now left the building<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>1. Proablly your fuel injectors.  Also, your new (rebuilt) engine will get pretty bad gas milage during break-in, if its not already broken in. I'd get a set of new injectors for a 350 chevy TPI engine, and an adjustable fuel press. regulator. <P>2. My 2.8 auto 3spd runs about 3000 rpms @ 75 mph, not sure on the km/h conversion, but thats what mine does.<P>3. This shouldn't cause a problem...Many have done it..I haven't, but I know tons who have.<P>4. Lock-up silinoid or however you spell it...||||reg||1
